How to fix:
Perform a real user-authentication step instead of expecting a token string. Require the owner wrapping key in `AndroidKeyStore` to be created with per-use user authentication (`setUserAuthenticationParameters(0, AUTH_BIOMETRIC_STRONG or AUTH_DEVICE_CREDENTIAL)`) and initialize its cipher through a `BiometricPrompt` `CryptoObject`, so unwrap fails at the platform level unless the user authenticated. Pass the resulting authenticated key handle into `KeystoreKeyVault` rather than a caller-asserted credential, and remove the token parameter from `wrapKey`, `unwrapKey`, the engine entry points and the UI so no caller can assert its own authorization. Keep the non-owner operator/presence keys on their current no-unlock wrapping key so background audits continue to work.

Please fix this vulnerability. If you propose a fix, make it concise and minimal.
