### 🔴 Checkpoint proposer can move committee seats by forging the unverified `seat_participation` record

**Severity:** HIGH · **CWE-345**

A checkpoint block's `seat_participation` record is authored by the block proposer and is never checked against the finality certificate that proves which validators actually signed. `derive_seat_table_for_checkpoint` (src/chain/blockchain.rs:7844) feeds the peer-supplied record straight into `CommitteeTable::hand_over`, which hands any seat missing from both of two consecutive records to its standby and adds the displaced validator to the epoch's `lost` set. A proposer that produces two consecutive checkpoint blocks can publish records omitting seats whose holders did vote, silently evicting up to `ceil(S/10)` seats per checkpoint from validators that never missed a vote; a single such block can equally suppress a legitimate handover by writing `None` or an all-ones bitmap. The derived table is what later certificates are verified against (`verify_with_committee` counts `covered_seats` against `quorum_seats` from it), so committee composition and the finality quorum denominator become proposer-controlled. The branch head does not compile, so this is a source-level trace rather than a dynamic proof.

```suggestion
