### 🟢 Presence aggregates accepted for any window: stale proof replay keeps an offline validator earning and unsuspended

**Severity:** LOW

PresenceTracker::apply_aggregate verifies the block-embedded BLS aggregate for whatever `aggregate.window` the aggregate itself carries, but never checks it against `window_of_epoch(current_epoch, class)` and never requires monotonicity: the `last_seen_window != Some(aggregate.window)` guard lets an older window through and then sets `last_seen_epoch = current_epoch` and increments `seen_windows_in_period`. A validator that has stopped signing can therefore have any previously valid aggregate replayed to look present every epoch, defeating the `absent_epochs >= threshold_epochs` suspension test in `advance_epoch` (a suspended validator stops holding duties and stops earning) and inflating `reward_multiplier_ppm`. Identified from source review only: the new presence module has no production caller yet (`apply_aggregate`, `advance_epoch` and `reward_multiplier_ppm` are unreferenced outside `xtask/` static gates and `tests/rehearsal`), and the branch head does not compile, so the impact is latent until the block-execution presence hook is wired.

