### 🟢 EE host writes are not bound to the calling environment's namespace

**Severity:** LOW

**TL;DR:** `HostApi::write` on `HostBridge` (src/execution/coordinator/mod.rs:868) hands the caller-chosen namespace straight to `TxOverlay::write`, which only checks that the namespace is a known UEL root group, so any environment may stage writes into another environment's state.

**Impact:** An EE worker process that is faulty or replaced can forge state owned by other environments — EVM/SVM accounts, `uel/assets` custody records, `uel/alias` entries — and have those writes committed with the block; no reachable path lets a contract author or transaction sender choose a namespace today.

**Root cause:**
- The host treats state-write policy as something it must enforce itself (gas, static frames, balance debits are all re-checked host-side) but leaves namespace selection entirely to the caller of `HostApi::write`, so no layer binds a write to the environment that issued it.
- `HostBridge::write` forwards `ns` unchanged to `TxOverlay::write`, which validates only `is_static()` and `RootGroup::for_namespace(ns).is_some()` — the frame's own environment is stored on `FrameSnapshot::ee` and never compared against the namespace being written.
- The worker transport passes a worker-supplied namespace string into the same path, validating only the character set, so a process on the other end of the EE socket can name `ee/evm/account`, `ee/svm/account`, `ue/assets` or `uel/alias` freely.
- Severity is limited to this level because every shipped write site (in-process EVM/WASM/SVM/Move/BudZero adapters and the `budlum-ee-*` workers under `execution/`) uses a compile-time constant namespace of its own group, and contract-visible host functions such as CosmWasm `db_write` accept only key and value — no attacker-controlled path currently selects a namespace.

```suggestion
    fn write(&mut self, ns: &Namespace, key: &[u8], value: Option<&[u8]>) -> Result<(), HostError> {
        use crate::execution::coordinator::state::RootGroup;
        let group = RootGroup::for_namespace(ns.as_str());
        let owned = match self.frame_actor.ee {
            EeId::EVM => group == Some(RootGroup::Evm),
            EeId::WASM => group == Some(RootGroup::Wasm),
            EeId::SVM => group == Some(RootGroup::Svm),
            EeId::MOVE => group == Some(RootGroup::Move),
            EeId::BUDZERO => group == Some(RootGroup::BudZero),
            _ => false,
        };
        if !owned {
            return Err(HostError::Denied(format!(
                "execution environment 0x{:02x} may not write namespace `{}`",
                self.frame_actor.ee.0,
                ns.as_str()
            )));
        }
        self.overlay.write(ns.as_str(), key, value)
    }
```

