### 🟠 Unbounded native recursion in EVM intra-call path (zero-value CALL) crashes the node

**Severity:** HIGH

**TL;DR:** In `run_evm_bytecode` (src/execution/coordinator/evm_ee.rs) a zero-value `CALL` recurses into `dispatch_evm_target` → `run_evm_bytecode` with no frame-depth counter, so a self-calling contract exhausts the thread stack.

**Impact:** Any account able to deploy EVM bytecode can deploy a contract whose code calls itself and halt the chain: the recursion overflows the native stack and aborts the node process (not a catchable panic) on every node that executes the transaction.

**Root cause:**
- Intra-environment EVM calls are implemented as native Rust recursion instead of an explicit, bounded frame stack, so the only limit on call depth is the shared gas counter, which is far too coarse to stop stack exhaustion.
- The depth counter that does exist — `MAX_UNIVERSAL_CALL_DEPTH = 8` enforced in `TxOverlay::push_universal_frame` — is only reached through `HostApi::universal_call` (the non-zero-value branch), and `EeCall.depth` is never read anywhere in `evm_ee.rs`.
- The zero-value branch charges only the 3-gas loop fee plus the operand pushes (about 24 gas per level), so a 30M BGU limit permits roughly a million levels while a few thousand native frames already overflow the stack; the `catch_unwind` in `worker.rs` cannot catch a stack overflow, so the process aborts.

```suggestion
fn run_evm_bytecode(
    frame: EvmBytecodeCall<'_>,
    host: &mut dyn HostApi,
) -> Result<(OutcomeStatus, Vec<u8>), String> {
    thread_local! {
        static EVM_FRAME_DEPTH: std::cell::Cell<u32> = std::cell::Cell::new(0);
    }
    struct DepthGuard;
    impl DepthGuard {
        fn enter() -> Result<Self, String> {
            EVM_FRAME_DEPTH.with(|depth| {
                let next = depth.get().saturating_add(1);
                if next > 1_024 {
                    return Err(String::from("call depth exceeded"));
                }
                depth.set(next);
                Ok(Self)
            })
        }
    }
    impl Drop for DepthGuard {
        fn drop(&mut self) {
            EVM_FRAME_DEPTH.with(|depth| depth.set(depth.get().saturating_sub(1)));
        }
    }
    let _depth_guard = DepthGuard::enter()?;
    let EvmBytecodeCall {
        ctx,
        self_addr,
        caller20,
        value_wei,
        code,
        calldata,
        is_static,
        gas_limit,
    } = frame;
```

