### 🟡 Wallet `.bud` verification trusts a root and epoch taken from the node's own proof answer, so a lying node chooses the transfer recipient

**Severity:** MEDIUM

**TL;DR:** `verify_bns_recipient_proof` (`crates/wallet-core/src/bns.rs`) checks the `.bud` Merkle branch only against a caller-supplied root and epoch, and `wallet-core` offers no header-verified source for either.

**Impact:** A wallet host using this crate's own RPC surface passes the `bns_root` and `epoch` from `bud_bnsGetProof`, so a lying node can answer with a self-consistent proof and the user signs a transfer to the attacker's address while the screen shows the `.bud` name they typed.

**Root cause:**
- The function takes the root and epoch as ordinary arguments, so "header-committed" is an assumption about the caller: `wallet-core` has no header type, no header request and no header verification, and nothing else in the crate yields a `bns_v1` root.
- The only root and epoch channel the crate models is `bud_bnsGetProof` (`crates/wallet-core/src/rpc.rs`), which returns `bns_root`, `epoch` and the branch in one object, so a node that invents a root invents the matching branch and epoch with it.
- An empty branch is accepted and the registry root is recomputed with the proof's own `meta_digest`, so any owner, address and expiry fold to whatever root the same answer names; `UnsignedTransfer::to_verified_bud_recipient` then puts that address into the signed transfer.

```suggestion
/// A `bns_v1` registry root and the epoch of the header it was read from,
/// authenticated against a chain header the wallet has accepted.
///
/// The fields are private and there is no public constructor, so an answer to
/// `bud_bnsGetProof` - which carries `bns_root`, `epoch` and the branch in one
/// object - cannot be turned into an anchor: a node that invents the root would
/// invent the matching epoch and branch with it.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct VerifiedBnsAnchor {
    root: [u8; 32],
    epoch: u64,
}

impl VerifiedBnsAnchor {
    /// Built only by the header-validation path, once `bns_v1` has been read
    /// out of a header the wallet accepted.
    #[must_use]
    pub(crate) fn from_validated_header(root: [u8; 32], epoch: u64) -> Self {
        Self { root, epoch }
    }
}

/// Verify a `.bud` Merkle proof against a header-authenticated anchor and
/// return the authenticated recipient address.
///
/// * If `proof.extras_preimage` is `Some(bytes)`, verifies `BDLM_BNS_EXTRAS_V1`
///   and extracts the authenticated `record.address` forwarding target (failing
///   closed if `record.address` was cleared or zero).
/// * If `proof.extras_preimage` is `None`, returns the authenticated `owner`
///   only when `claimed_target == proof.owner`.
///
/// # Errors
///
/// Refuses invalid names, expired leaves (`expires_at <= anchor.epoch`), root
/// mismatches, zero addresses, or unauthenticated target substitution.
pub fn verify_bns_recipient_proof(
    requested_name: &str,
    claimed_target: &[u8; 32],
    proof: &WalletBnsProof,
    anchor: &VerifiedBnsAnchor,
) -> Result<[u8; 32], String> {
    if !is_valid_bud_name(requested_name) {
        return Err(format!("invalid .bud name '{requested_name}'"));
    }
    if proof.name != requested_name {
        return Err("proof name does not match requested .bud name".into());
    }
    if *claimed_target == [0u8; 32] || proof.owner == [0u8; 32] {
        return Err("BNS owner or target address cannot be the zero address".into());
    }
    if proof.expires_at <= anchor.epoch {
        return Err("proven .bud name has expired at the verified header epoch".into());
    }
    let leaf = compute_bns_leaf_digest(
        &proof.name,
        &proof.owner,
        proof.expires_at,
        proof.content_id.as_ref(),
        proof.storage_root.as_ref(),
        &proof.extras_digest,
    );
    let names_root = fold_bns_merkle_branch(leaf, &proof.siblings, &proof.directions)
        .ok_or_else(|| "malformed BNS Merkle branch".to_string())?;
    let computed_root = compute_bns_registry_root(&proof.meta_digest, &names_root);
    if computed_root != anchor.root {
        return Err("BNS Merkle proof did not reproduce expected header bns_root".into());
    }
```

