### 🟡 BNS non-inclusion proof verifier accepts one non-adjacent boundary branch, so a prover can certify any registered `.bud` name as absent

**Severity:** MEDIUM

**TL;DR:** The absence arm of `BnsRegistry::verify_state_proof` (`src/bns/registry.rs`) accepts a single boundary branch under any name that merely sorts next to the target, so an honest inclusion branch of another name can be relabelled to prove a registered name absent.

**Impact:** A node or peer serving `.bud` proofs can make any verifying wallet, browser or SDK host believe a live, owned name is unregistered, so that client treats a taken name as free and unclaimed while its own header-committed root says otherwise.

**Root cause:**
- Non-existence is decided from the lexicographic order of the two disclosed branch names instead of from an authenticated commitment to leaf positions, so every branch in the same tree satisfies the check for any target name sorting after or before it.
- The arm accepts a single boundary (`predecessor` or `successor` alone) and never relates the two branches when both are supplied, and `proof.names_count` is never bound to the leaf, so leaves 0 and N-1 can stand in for a neighbour pair.
- `build_branch_at` emits only siblings and directions - no leaf index and no count - so the verifier has no position information to check adjacency with, although the module documents `prove_name`/`verify_state_proof` as producing "adjacent boundary non-existence proofs".

```suggestion
        } else {
            if proof.entry.is_some() {
                return Err("non-inclusion proof must not carry an entry branch".into());
            }
            if proof.names_count == 0 {
                if proof.predecessor.is_some() || proof.successor.is_some() {
                    return Err("empty registry proof cannot carry boundary branches".into());
                }
                if Self::root_from_parts(proof.meta_digest, [0u8; 32]) != *expected_bns_root {
                    return Err("empty registry root mismatch".into());
                }
                return Ok(None);
            }
            // Absence is only proven by two adjacent leaves, or by one leaf at
            // either end of the tree. Recover the index each boundary was built
            // at from its `directions` and the committed tree shape: a branch
            // whose name merely sorts next to the target proves nothing.
            let leaf_index = |dirs: &[bool]| -> Option<u64> {
                let mut sizes = vec![proof.names_count];
                while *sizes.last()? > 1 {
                    sizes.push(sizes.last()?.div_ceil(2));
                }
                let mut index: u64 = 0;
                let mut used = 0usize;
                for level in (0..sizes.len().saturating_sub(1)).rev() {
                    if 2 * index + 1 < sizes[level] {
                        let step = dirs.len().checked_sub(1 + used)?;
                        let dir = *dirs.get(step)?;
                        used += 1;
                        index = 2 * index + u64::from(dir);
                    } else {
                        index *= 2;
                    }
                }
                (used == dirs.len()).then_some(index)
            };
            let predecessor_index = match &proof.predecessor {
                Some(pred) => {
                    if pred.name.as_str() >= proof.name.as_str() {
                        return Err("predecessor name is not strictly less than target".into());
                    }
                    let root = check_branch(pred)?;
                    if Self::root_from_parts(proof.meta_digest, root) != *expected_bns_root {
                        return Err("predecessor branch did not reproduce expected bns_root".into());
                    }
                    Some(leaf_index(&pred.directions).ok_or_else(|| {
                        "predecessor branch is not a leaf of the committed tree".to_string()
                    })?)
                }
                None => None,
            };
            let successor_index = match &proof.successor {
                Some(succ) => {
                    if succ.name.as_str() <= proof.name.as_str() {
                        return Err("successor name is not strictly greater than target".into());
                    }
                    let root = check_branch(succ)?;
                    if Self::root_from_parts(proof.meta_digest, root) != *expected_bns_root {
                        return Err("successor branch did not reproduce expected bns_root".into());
                    }
                    Some(leaf_index(&succ.directions).ok_or_else(|| {
                        "successor branch is not a leaf of the committed tree".to_string()
                    })?)
                }
                None => None,
            };
            let adjacent = match (predecessor_index, successor_index) {
                (Some(pred_idx), Some(succ_idx)) => succ_idx == pred_idx + 1,
                (Some(pred_idx), None) => pred_idx + 1 == proof.names_count,
                (None, Some(succ_idx)) => succ_idx == 0,
                (None, None) => false,
            };
            if !adjacent {
                return Err("boundary branches are not adjacent leaves of the committed tree".into());
            }
            Ok(None)
