### 🔵 dApp website URL gate accepts raw markup and entity-encoded `javascript:` schemes

**Severity:** LOW

**TL;DR:** `is_valid_app_url` in `src/budlumxyz/mod.rs` looks for a colon only before the first `/`, so `<script>alert(1)</script>` and `javascript&colon;alert(1)` pass as app URLs and are stored and served unchecked.

**Impact:** Any funded account can publish an app whose `website_url` is markup or an entity-encoded `javascript:` URL, served to every client through the public `bud_hubGetApps` call, so a wallet or explorer that renders it inherits script execution.

**Root cause:**
- The validator treats "no colon before the first slash" as "no scheme, therefore safe" instead of parsing the whole string, so acceptance is the function's default branch rather than the outcome of a check.
- `let head_end = trimmed.find('/').unwrap_or(trimmed.len())` limits the scheme search to the prefix before the first `/`, and a value with no literal `:` at all returns `true`, accepting `<script>alert(1)</script>`, `//evil.example/x` and `javascript&colon;alert(1)`.
- `register_app` copies the raw input into `AppRecord.website_url` and `bud_hubGetApps` returns every record unfiltered, so the accepted bytes are exactly what clients receive.

```suggestion
fn is_valid_app_url(url: &str) -> bool {
    if url.is_empty() || url.len() > MAX_APP_URL_BYTES || url != url.trim() {
        return false;
    }
    if url.chars().any(char::is_control) {
        return false;
    }
    // Parse the whole string, never a prefix. A `/` before the `:` (or no
    // literal `:` at all) is not "scheme-less and therefore safe":
    // `javascript&colon;alert(1)` and `<script>alert(1)</script>` reach a
    // renderer as a live scheme or as markup. Only an absolute URL on one of
    // the three content/transport schemes is accepted, so the default for
    // every other shape is refusal.
    let Some((scheme, rest)) = url.split_once("://") else {
        return false;
    };
    if rest.is_empty()
        || rest.starts_with('/')
        || rest.chars().any(char::is_whitespace)
        || rest.chars().any(char::is_control)
    {
        return false;
    }
    scheme.eq_ignore_ascii_case("https")
        || scheme.eq_ignore_ascii_case("bud")
        || scheme.eq_ignore_ascii_case("ipfs")
}
```

