### 🟡 Paid view receipts are written into consensus state with no cap and no prune path, so any funded account can grow the registry and every block's state root without limit

**Severity:** MEDIUM · Deep review

**TL;DR:** `Bud3Registry::record_paid_view` (src/storage/bud3/registry.rs:649) adds a receipt to a consensus map that nothing ever prunes: `paid_at_epoch` is written but never read, and receipts outlive the object they name.

**Impact:** Any account holding 100 atoms can append a permanent record that every node stores, re-hashes in every block's state root and serialises into every snapshot, so a few hundred BUD of receipts slows block validation and pushes snapshots past their 512 MiB read ceiling for all node operators.

**Root cause:**
- ["The paid fallback-view door prices a receipt as a single 100-atom fee, a tenth of the protocol's own `MIN_STORAGE_FEE_BUD`, and gives the stored record no lifetime, so permanent consensus state is sold without rent or expiry.", "`record_paid_view` inserts into `paid_views` with no cap per object, per payer or in total, and neither `expire` nor `drop_object` removes entries, so `paid_at_epoch` is dead weight and every receipt ever paid stays rooted.", "`Bud3Registry::state_root` refolds every receipt on each call with no cached tree, unlike the account set's `cached_tree`, so each entry is a permanent per-block hashing cost on every node."]

```suggestion
/// Minimum fee in BUD base units required for G8 validator fallback decoding
/// (`0.0001 BUD` = `100` base units at `10^6` scale, Section 6.5 G8).
pub const MIN_PAID_VIEW_FEE_ATOMS: u64 = 100;

/// Epochs a paid view receipt stays in consensus state after payment.
///
/// A receipt authorises one decode; one that was never presented inside this
/// window is dropped by `Bud3Registry::expire` instead of being folded into the
/// state root, kept in the snapshot and hashed again on every block forever.
pub const PAID_VIEW_RETENTION_EPOCHS: u64 = 30 * super::fees::DEFAULT_EPOCHS_PER_DAY;
```

