```

How to fix:
Give the receipt a lifetime in consensus state. Prune `paid_views` in the per-epoch sweep using `paid_at_epoch`, and drop the receipts of an object when that object is deleted or expires, so the map is bounded by a retention window and by the live objects rather than by everything ever paid.

Pick the retention window to cover the usable life of a one-decode receipt and have the view gateway treat receipts near the window's end as expired, so a pruned receipt is refused rather than silently accepted. If a longer lifetime is required, price it: charge a per-epoch rent for keeping a receipt rooted, or raise the fee to the storage-fee floor and commit the entry's lifetime into the receipt, rather than leaving an unbounded permanent write at a flat price.

